            [Constants]
                'Every present COM port as (port, friendly_name) pairs, e.g.\n\t(\'COM3\', \'USB-SERIAL CH340 (COM3)\'). Used by the RP2040 connection\n\tdialog\'s "List Ports" button (see KmboxConfigDialog\'s "rp2040" branch\n\tbelow).\n\n\tDeliberately self-contained (its own SetupDi/ctypes bindings) instead of\n\treusing the "Shared Win32 serial-port plumbing" further down this file\n\t(near the KMBOX B+/Ferrum drivers, e.g. _serial_setupapi/_ferrum_detect_\n\tport()) - that section is defined much later in the file, and this\n\tneeds to run during the startup input-method picker, long before\n\texecution ever reaches it. The KMBOX B+/Ferrum dialogs never hit this\n\tproblem because they only call their own port-scan helpers at actual\n\tconnect time (inside _init_hardware_backend, called after the whole\n\tmodule has finished loading), never during dialog construction.'
