                10      STORE_NAME                      2: __qualname__
                12      LOAD_CONST                      1: 'QScrollArea with velocity/friction momentum scrolling on the mouse\n\twheel - a direct port of this project\'s own www/smoothscroll.js, not a\n\tgeneric "ease to a fixed target" animation. Each wheel tick ADDS to a\n\tpersistent velocity (it doesn\'t compute a destination up front), and a\n\t~60fps timer integrates that velocity into the scroll position every\n\tframe, decaying it by a friction factor each tick until it drops below\n\ta stop threshold. Quick repeated wheel ticks compound the velocity\n\t(scrolls farther/faster) and the view keeps gliding briefly after you\n\tstop scrolling, exactly like the JS version - not a fixed-duration ease.\n\t'
