                'Runs the input-method handshake for the current MYEVENTER; on\n\tfailure, shows a popup and sends the user back to the input-method\n\tpicker to try again, instead of crashing (RP2350) or silently opening\n\tthe app with a dead backend (KMBOX/Ferrum). Updates the module-level\n\tMYEVENTER to whatever was ultimately picked, and only returns once\n\t_init_hardware_backend() actually succeeded for it.\n\n\tCBuild\'s own handshake doesn\'t happen here - client.DriverMouse.connect()\n\tonly gets called later, deep inside Ai992.__init__ - so a CBuild pick\n\talways "succeeds" at this stage; see the retry loop there for its\n\tpopup-and-reselect handling.'
